+# Veterinarian Directory Filtering, Not Free-Text Search
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined search for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, leaving only owners searchable. A request then arrived to let a reader narrow the veterinarian directory to a single specialty — an attribute the directory already displays next to each veterinarian.
+
+That request forces a distinction NG-9 blurred. Free-text search over veterinarians — typing a fragment and matching it against names or other fields — is one capability. Filtering an already-listed collection by a value the page already shows is a different, narrower one. NG-9 as written declined both.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-9 whole** — decline all veterinarian search and filtering alike; refuse the request.
+2. **Withdraw NG-9 for veterinarians** — allow veterinarian search of every kind, free-text included.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** — free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope; filtering the directory by an attribute it already displays comes into scope.
+
+## Decision
+
+Option 3. Free-text veterinarian search remains a non-goal. Filtering the directory by a specialty it already shows is in scope, realized by `REQ-VET-003`. The line NG-9 draws is now between searching for a veterinarian and narrowing a directory the reader is already looking at.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The directory gains a filter without opening a general search surface, so the demonstration stays small — the reason NG-9 existed.
+- NG-9 now draws a finer line: a reader must see that filtering a displayed attribute is permitted while free-text search is not. The row and this ADR carry that distinction together.
+- The machine-readable form of the directory becomes a supported surface under the same requirement, since the filter applies to both surfaces the directory is published on.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9 (narrowed) — realized by [`REQ-VET-003`](../prd.md#req-vet-003).
+
+## References
+
+- [prd.md § Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — NG-9, the narrowed row
+- [prd.md § Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — `REQ-VET-003`, the filter capability
