 ### Veterinarian directory
 
-<a id="req-vet-001"></a>
+<a id="req-vet-001"></a><a id="req-vet-003"></a>
 
-The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`.
+The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`. The same directory is also published in a machine-readable form at a second route, and that route is a supported surface `[REQ-VET-003]`.
+
+Both surfaces accept an optional specialty filter. Given a specialty, only the veterinarians holding it are shown — on the page still a page at a time, and in the machine-readable form as the matching veterinarians alone. The filter matches the whole specialty name and disregards letter case; a value that is only the start of a specialty name does not match, unlike owner search. A specialty no veterinarian holds returns the normal result with an empty veterinarian list rather than an error. An empty or whitespace-only filter is treated as no filter, the same way an empty owner search returns every owner (`REQ-OWN-002`). Without the filter, both surfaces behave as they do today `[REQ-VET-003]`.
 
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each name and its specialties are listed a page at a time.
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown as having none.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the directory is requested in its machine-readable form, then that route returns the same veterinarians and their specialties as a supported surface.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty that at least one veterinarian holds, when the directory page is filtered by that specialty, then only the veterinarians holding it are listed, still a page at a time.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty that at least one veterinarian holds, when the machine-readable form is filtered by that specialty, then only the veterinarians holding it are returned.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty name differing from a held specialty only by letter case, when either surface is filtered by it, then it matches; given a value that is only the start of a specialty name, when either surface is filtered by it, then it does not match.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty no veterinarian holds, when either surface is filtered by it, then the normal result is returned with an empty veterinarian list and a successful response, not an error.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given an empty or whitespace-only filter value, when either surface is requested, then it behaves as if no filter were supplied.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given no specialty filter, when either surface is requested, then it behaves exactly as `REQ-VET-001` specifies.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. A veterinarian's specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
-2. **Known defect.** A second route returns the same list in a machine-readable form. Nothing consumes it, and it carries no requirement — see the Superseded list.
+2. The directory is also published in a machine-readable form at a second route. That route is a supported surface under `REQ-VET-003`; it was previously an unrequested artifact, whose earlier standing is recorded in the Superseded list under `REQ-VET-002`.
 
 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
